{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"4623aeb65367af44ac3f492f35afe35f2a50099faacf72b74fa6c5bb5ef0e810","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I found two issues: the length filter was discarding tessellated eave edges under 30 cm, and surviving points were getting blocked by the roof's own underside. I'll fix this by emitting along short edges by length and only letting upward-facing surfaces (like a lower roof, sill, or gutter) stop a drop, which also eliminates false eaves from mid-roof tile rows.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LgfjVqViqL5DFZECHZWdfe","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && sed -n 100,175p js/drips.js","description":"Re-read the eave extraction code"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
