{"parentUuid":"cda8c4e1-ef46-437e-867d-d695d96cf984","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgG1HAjF3mNUT2BeZr5p2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N7H9Zxc28sdCuqfne6x9Tt","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='js/drips.js'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"   to the ground, or to the part of the building below (a lower roof, a\n   sill). Each point lets a drop go every second or few, and the drops are\n   worked out on the GPU: free fall from rest, drifting with the wind, drawn\n   as a streak the length of its blur, lit like the rain by the lamps, the\n   fires, a flare and the lightning, hidden behind what stands in front. */\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"   to the ground, or to the part of the building below (a lower roof, a\n   sill). Each point's whole fall is one thin ribbon, and its shader works\n   out where the water is on it now: the water at a height left the edge as\n   long ago as it takes to fall that far, so drops speed up and their blur\n   stretches as they go. Most points drip, a drop every second or so; where\n   water runs together (one in seven) it pours as a string that leaves the\n   edge whole and breaks into drops further down. Lit like the rain by the\n   lamps, the fires, a flare and the lightning, hidden behind what stands in\n   front. */\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nnode --check js/drips.js && REDACTED && node $S/hl.mjs eval $S/reload.js >/dev/null; sleep 2; node $S/hl.mjs eval $S/boot.js >/dev/null && node $S/hl.mjs eval $S/helpers.js >/dev/null && cat > $S/v_drip4.js <<'EOF'\nwindow.__views = [['wide', 0.5, 92, 0.0, 0.1], ['church', 6, 125, 0.3, 0.2], ['barn', -2, 80, 0.8, 0.1], ['wallrun', 4.0, 92, 0.15, 0.1]]; window.__tag = 'fin'; return 1;\nEOF\nnode $S/hl.mjs eval $S/v_drip4.js >/dev/null && node $S/hl.mjs eval $S/dr1.js | tr -d '\\n'; echo; cd $S/snaps && python3 -c \"\nfrom PIL import Image\nW=Image.new('RGB',(2048,1536))\nfor i,n in enumerate(['wide','church','barn','wallrun']): W.paste(Image.open(f'dr1_{n}_fin.jpg'),((i%2)*1024,(i//2)*768))\nW.resize((1536,1152)).save('dr1_fin.jpg')\n\"","description":"Update the header and capture wider views"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1950,"cache_read_input_tokens":690057,"output_tokens":1167,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":127},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1950,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1167,"cache_read_input_tokens":690057,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1950,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1950},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01N7H9Zxc28sdCuqfne6x9Tt":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 - <<'PY'\np='js/drips.js'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"   to the ground, or to the part of the building below (a lower roof, a\n   sill). Each point lets a drop go every second or few, and the drops are\n   worked out on the GPU: free fall from rest, drifting with the wind, drawn\n   as a streak the length of its blur, lit like the rain by the lamps, the\n   fires, a flare and the lightning, hidden behind what stands in front. */\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"   to the ground, or to the part of the building below (a lower roof, a\n   sill). Each point's whole fall is one thin ribbon, and its shader works\n   out where the water is on it now: the water at a height left the edge as\n   long ago as it takes to fall that far, so drops speed up and their blur\n   stretches as they go. Most points 