"... and 1 more (truncated for prompt size)\"],\"denyWithinAllow\":[\"/Users/vojta/.claude/settings.json\",\"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/settings.json\",\"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/settings.local.json\",\"/tmp/claude-501/claude-settings-a31c3b004c1221a0.json\",\"/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed-settings.json\",\"/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed-settings.d\",\"REDACTED.claude/settings.json\",\"REDACTED.claude/settings.local.json\",\"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/skills\",\"REDACTED.claude/skills\",\"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/hooks\",\"REDACTED.claude/hooks\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/local\",\"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/.cc-writes\",\"REDACTED.claude/.cc-writes\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/.cc-writes\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/jobs\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/seed-admin\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/daemon\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/bridge-spawn\",\"/private/tmp/claude-501/bash-edit-diff\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/shell-snapshots\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/session-env\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/plugins\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/hooks\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/skills\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/workflows\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/commands\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/agents\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/routines\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/rules\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/output-styles\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/launch.json\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/CLAUDE.md\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/projects\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/daemon.json\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/policy-limits.json\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/policy-limits.json.signature.json\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/policy-limits.json.signature-iat.json\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/policy-limits.json.stamp.json\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/backups\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/loop.md\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/cowork_plugins\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/dev-mods\",\"REDACTED\",\"/Users/vojta/Library/Application REDACTED\",\"/Users/vojta/Library/Application REDACTED\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/mcp-skill-archives\",\"/Users/vojta/.claude/mcp-discovery-cache\",\"... and 129 more (truncated for prompt size)\"]}}\n\n - You should always default to running commands within the sandbox. Do NOT attempt to set `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` unless:\n  - The user *explicitly* asks you to bypass sandbox\n  - A specific command just failed and you see evidence of sandbox restrictions causing the failure. Note that commands can fail for many reasons unrelated to the sandbox (missing files, wrong arguments, network issues, etc.).\n - Evidence of sandbox-caused failures includes:\n  - \"Operation not permitted\" errors for file/network operations\n  - Access denied to specific paths outside allowed directories\n  - Network connection failures to non-whitelisted hosts\n  - Unix socket connection errors\n - When you see evidence of sandbox-caused failure:\n  - If the `<sandbox_violations>` block names a denied host, re-run the command with that host in its `allowed_domains` (auto mode); otherwise retry with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` directly rather than asking in prose first — the retry itself goes through the permission gate (a user prompt, or the auto-mode classifier when auto mode is active)\n  - Briefly explain what sandbox restriction likely caused the failure. Be sure to mention that the user can use the `/sandbox` command to change the sandbox settings.\n - A sandbox denial on a credential, a file or a host that the task does not involve is the boundary above at work: tell the user rather than retrying with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true`.\n - Treat each command you execute with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` individually. Even if you have recently run a command with this setting, you should default to running future commands within the sandbox.\n - Do not suggest adding sensitive paths like ~/.bashrc, ~/.zshrc, ~/.ssh/*, or credential files to the sandbox allowlist.\n - Network egress goes through a filtering proxy. Attempt requests and read the error rather than predicting whether a host is reachable; denied connections are reported in a `<sandbox_violations>` block explaining the reason. In auto mode, list the hosts a command needs beyond that in its `allowed_domains` — a denied host named in the block goes there on the re-run.\n - Opening an app, file or URL with `open`, or scripting another app with `osascript`, is blocked inside this sandbox (macOS Launch Services and Apple Events are off) and fails with errors such as -10822 (kLSServerCommunicationErr), -54, -600 or \"LSOpenURLsWithRole() failed\". That failure is the sandbox, not a problem with what you built; do not retry it with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true`. Tell the user the sandbox blocked it and give them the exact command to run themselves.\n - For temporary files, always use the `$TMPDIR` environment variable. TMPDIR is automatically set to the correct sandbox-writable directory in sandbox mode. Do NOT use `/tmp` directly - use `$TMPDIR` instead."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"304f353b-08ae-4072-bc9d-a193a62999e0","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:32:54.491Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n## Bash command sandbox\nBy default, Bash commands run inside an OS-level sandbox (macOS Seatbelt) applied to each command separately, not to the session as a whole; how it is configured in this session is described below.\n\nThe sandbox marks out what this session was given: the directories listed below, the network destinations the task involves, and the credentials the user supplied for it. Treat that as the boundary even where a limit below is not enforced. Commands can reach more than that — credentials and keys elsewhere on this machine, the user's other projects and configuration, sockets that control this machine or other workloads, cloud metadata endpoints — but being reachable does not make them provided; those are the user's, not the task's, unless the user's request calls for t