{"parentUuid":"dcf15dbf-ba8a-43e9-a4f1-90cea38a4bf6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgG28FBVvENeQEmsZwr1J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added three more commits to `hedgerow-grass` this round. Nothing is pushed, the branch still merges cleanly into `hedgerow-poc`, and the four first-person files (camera, player, hud, character) are untouched.\n\n- **378cd410 – rain drips and pours off the eaves.** New file `drips.js`. When the level loads it finds the roof edges in the house, church and barn models (about 3,600 drip points across the village, 46 ms to find). Water falls from each point to the ground or onto the part of the building below. Most points drip; about one in seven pours a thin string of water that breaks into drops further down. It's most visible near a lamp, falling in front of a door or a shop front; from further away it stays subtle. It costs 0.2–0.5 ms per frame near houses on the test machine. To support it, `levelBuild.js` now also returns the list of placed props.\n- **808ded9b – the drips splash where they land.** Within 9 m, each drop throws up a small crown of droplets as it hits the ground, using the same look as the rain's own splashes.\n- **58c4ef5b – explosions throw solid clods and stones.** New file `chunks.js`. Grenades and charges now throw real tumbling lumps (mud clods in the fields, stones on the cobbles) that bounce and stay where they land. The old flat debris sprites are now just fine dirt specks, except in water. At night the gain is modest: the pieces mostly read as dark shapes against the fireball. The dark star-shaped blobs you'll see after a close blast are the existing mud-on-the-lens effect, not debris.\n\nAll three quality presets compile without shader errors and the node checks pass. The test server and headless browser are stopped and my `launch.json` entry is removed. Each commit is logged in the shared notes file, `hedgerow-grass-session.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":231,"cache_read_input_tokens":760565,"output_tokens":602,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":231,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":602,"cache_read_input_tokens":760565,"cache_creation_input_tokens":231,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":231},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a80fcede-79ba-4da2-94f7-032962fc8bfe","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgG28EU5pUpjKHpd8zXqC","requestRef":"cbb23112-c57d-476a-ac03-29a5dcc65e92","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"81c04710-7c4a-47a5-bea1-a2add2506e7e","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:33:38.804Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
