{"parentUuid":"40788953-d5c5-4e29-88f0-2c8de8a5155a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgG2N1zdXLKWZDgPsSvcH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W3uMTUnzUmtk14KBg3J1Er","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 - <<'PY'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"    (rain: near streaks a drop wide but never under a pixel and a half,\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"    (rain: near streaks a drop wide but never under a pixel and a half,\n    faint out in the dark and glittering by a lamp, a fire, a flare or the\n    lightning,\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nREDACTED; node $S/hl.mjs eval $S/q_chk2.js | tr -d '\\n '; echo; cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/README.md fun/hedgerow/js/weather.js && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: rain that shows where it is lit\n\nThe near rain streaks were drawn at the same opacity everywhere, so out in\nthe dark (a forest, a field) white needles covered the whole view as if lit\nby daylight. A drop out in the dark shows only the dark sky it refracts:\nan unlit streak now gets 45% of its old opacity (uUnlit), while the boost\nfrom the lamps, fires and the flare near it is as before, so rain still\nglitters by the lights. The lightning flash adds to it, lighting all the\nrain for its moment. The far sheets and the crowns were already dimmer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && git merge-tree --write-tree hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null && echo \"merges cleanly into hedgerow-poc\"","description":"Commit the lit-rain change"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":710,"cache_read_input_t