{"parentUuid":"add3731a-a28f-4ed4-b272-98cbe8f9bc1f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgG3esnMn8efJc1QBEeoY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added two more commits to `hedgerow-grass` this round. Nothing is pushed, the branch still merges cleanly into `hedgerow-poc`, and the four first-person files (camera, player, hud, character) are untouched.\n\n- **c5cb31f5 – muzzle smoke is a thin haze, not a glowing cloud.** Each shot left a large, fairly dense puff, and the next shot's flash lit it white. A Thompson or MG42 burst built a white cloud over the muzzle that hid the street and lingered afterwards. WWII ammunition left only a thin haze, so the puff is now darker, half as dense and a little smaller. I compared old and new on the same code, and the flash now reads as a crisp star with the street visible behind it.\n- **058c0569 – enemy tracers stop where they hit, and some ricochet.** A tracer that missed flew a full 150 m whatever it hit, just hidden behind walls and ground, so it never visibly ended at the impact. It now ends where the round strikes. A tracer glancing off stone, metal or a hard road (occasionally mud) skips on more slowly, often up into the sky, the classic look of night-fight footage. In a test burst, 4 of 17 tracers ricocheted.\n\nWhat I reviewed this round and left alone:\n- **No changes needed:** the street, square and meadow under a burning flare; a body after a kill; the MG nest up close; smoke over the burning truck; the far treeline.\n- **Left as is:** an enemy MG42 seen at about 5 m still shows as a white ball while it fires, because its flashes come back to back at 20 a second. It's stylised but clearly readable as enemy fire.\n- **Not a bug:** on the low preset, a dark line across one shop front turned out to be the awning rod, which just reads darker without the volumetric glow.\n\nAll three quality presets compile without shader errors, and I checked low and medium visually with all of this round's additions. The node checks pass. The test server and headless browser are stopped and my `launch.json` entry is removed. Each commit is logged in the shared notes file, `hedgerow-grass-session.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":244,"cache_read_input_tokens":879984,"output_tokens":700,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":244,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":700,"cache_read_input_tokens":879984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":244,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":244},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b60c9e87-ab09-4bdc-bf23-9e8f7155ae35","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgG3es5SwGa1zp6KLnuxQ","requestRef":"9a5a12dc-f471-4330-8c76-6fc3fa0fb0fc","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"caabb593-2290-44fd-afd9-362db72abd17","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:53:41.902Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
