{"parentUuid":"6bca19cb-b7da-4869-8bf3-fdb175ba81c2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgG4oe7hrrGFD4agfTMLe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013Nfh15oTz3a8rjzAwq6oQV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"    under a sky with no sun; the soldiers and their weapons keep it),\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"    under a sky with no sun; the soldiers and their weapons keep it),\n    `lightloop.js` (three.js shades every point light on every pixel, even\n    where its range has cut it to nothing; patched once at start, a light\n    that does not reach a pixel is skipped there - the same picture, the\n    frame some two and a half times quicker on the test GPU),\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/README.md fun/hedgerow/js/lightloop.js fun/hedgerow/js/main.js && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: point lights shade only the pixels they reach\n\nthree.js runs the whole direct-lighting path - BRDF, the skin/leaf/blade\nextras, the fill-glint test, the shadow lookup - for every point light on\nevery pixel of every lit material, even where the light's range has cut its\ncolour to exactly zero (and for the pool lights parked unused below the\nlevel). With the pool of eight plus the shadow light that is nine full\nshadings a pixel. lightloop.js patches THREE.ShaderChunk.lights_fragment_\nbegin once, before any material compiles, so a point light whose\ndirectLight.visible is false skips its shading and shadow lookup there.\n\nThe picture is unchanged (same-view captures of both builds match: square\n39.6/39.7, wall close-up 40.6/41.4 mean, the street differing only where the\nsearchlights moved). The GPU frame on the test machine went from ~40-45 ms\nto ~15-20 ms (street 43 -> 17-21, square 39 -> 15-16, meadow 38-45 -> 14-15),\nwhich the dynamic resolution turns into a sharper image on slower GPUs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && git merge-tree --write-tree hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null && echo \"merges cleanly into hedgerow-poc\"","description":"Commit the light-loop culling"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":516,"cache_read_input_tokens":959715,"output_tokens":927,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":516,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":927,"cache_read_input_tokens":959715,"cache_creation_input_tokens":516,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":516},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013Nfh15oTz3a8rjzAwq6oQV":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 - <<'PY'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"    under a sky with no sun; the soldiers and their weapons keep it),\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"    under a sky with no sun; the soldiers and their weapons keep it),\n    `lightloop.js` (three.js shades every point light on every pixel, even\n    where its range has cut it to nothing; patched once at start, a light\n    that does not reach a pixel is skipped there - the same picture, the\n    frame some two and a half times quicker on the test GPU),\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/README.md fun/hedgerow/js/lightloop.js fun/hedgerow/js/main.js && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: point lights shade only the pixels they reach\n\nthree.js runs the whole direct-lighting path - BRDF, the skin/leaf/blade\nextras, the fill-glint test, the shadow lookup - for every point light on\nevery pixel of every lit material, even where the light's range has cut its\ncolour to exactly zero (and for the pool lights parked unused below the\nlevel). With the pool of eight plus the shadow light that is nine full\nshadings a pixel. lightloop.js patches THREE.ShaderChunk.lights_fragment_\nbegin once, before any material compiles, so a point light whose\ndirectLight.visible is false skips its shading and shadow lookup there.\n\nThe picture is unchanged (same-view captures of both builds match: square\n39.6/39.7, wall close-up 40.6/41.4 mean, the street differing only where the\nsearchlights moved). The GPU frame on the test machine went from ~40-45 ms\nto ~15-20 ms (street 43 -> 17-21, square 39 -> 15-16, meadow 38-45 -> 14-15),\nwhich the dynamic resolution turns into a sharper image on slower GPUs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && git merge-tree --write-tree hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null && echo \"merges cleanly into hedgerow-poc\"","description":"Commit the light-loop culling"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_013Nfh15oTz3a8rjzAwq6oQV":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"8f673dc0-9191-480b-87ca-4a0197c642ea","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgG4odKKoRXrU1KZPWw8f","requestRef":"865b5303-a4ae-45b2-aa82-48a99b8d1037","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a82a1dae-d778-4212-9bb4-02f8e4af97eb","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:08:49.632Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedg