mmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"47ad52bf-d436-4572-912a-f84602d4848e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6d5c0a1d-fdd5-4db0-8cbd-a5c82a0adcb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W6YwTiMymnsz71CWYXSKkA","type":"tool_result","content":"- b4c41aa9 muzzle flashes vary per shot (effects.js muzzle(): size 0.65-1.35x, heat 0.6-1.2x).\n  Reviewed this round, fine: aiming down sights (the sight picture is the FP rig's), churchyard,\n  bridge (its parapet top is a smooth coping, not a texture bug), bunker, burning halftrack.\n\nTried and dropped: a second shadow-casting lamp (lights.js shadowLight2 for the next-strongest\nlamp/fire, high only). Subtle gain (sandbags shaded from the truck fire), but +10-15 ms a frame\n(street 43 -> 54 ms, square 39 -> 54 ms on the test GPU): every material lights each pixel with one\nmore point light and samples one more cube shadow. Redrawing the cube shadow map itself costs ~0.\nPerf note: per-pixel lighting with the 8-light pool + the shadow light is the main fragment cost;\nthe pool size is the big lever if frame time ever matters (fewer lights lit at once).\n\n- 94c82211 PERF (big): lightloop.js patches THREE.ShaderChunk.lights_fragment_begin at startup\n  (main.js calls cullPointLights() right after the imports) so a point light with\n  directLight.visible == false skips RE_Direct and its shadow lookup. Same picture; GPU frame\n  ~40-45 ms -> ~15-20 ms on the test machine. NOTE for three.js upgrades: it looks for\n  'getPointLightInfo( pointLight, geometryPosition, directLight );' and the next RE_Direct call;\n  does nothing if absent.\n\nMeasured: the meadow grass costs ~5.8-9.5 ms on this headless GPU at high quality looking across\nthe meadow (0.5 ms looking at the sky), and it scales with pixels (fragment-bound: shading the\nvisible blades with all the scene's lights). Drawing the tufts near-to-far made no measurable\ndifference (reverted). If frame time matters, the levers are the patch radius (quality.blades)\nor a cheaper lighting model for the blades.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4b711671-30e2-4b92-af38-2cd2f779ce23","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:14:36.715Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"- b4c41aa9 muzzle flashes vary per shot (effects.js muzzle(): size 0.65-1.35x, heat 0.6-1.2x).\n  Reviewed this round, fine: aiming down sights (the sight picture is the FP rig's), churchyard,\n  bridge (its parapet top is a smooth coping, not a texture bug), bunker, burning halftrack.\n\nTried and dropped: a second shadow-casting lamp (lights.js shadowLight2 for the next-strongest\nlamp/fire, high only). Subtle gain (sandbags shaded from the truck fire), but +10-15 ms a frame\n(street 43 -> 54 ms, square 39 -> 54 ms on the test GPU): every material lights each pixel with one\nmore point light and samples one more cube shadow. Redrawing the cube shadow map itself costs ~0.\nPerf note: per-pixel lighting with the 8-light pool + the shadow light is the main fragment cost;\nthe pool size is the big lever if frame time ever matters (fewer lights lit at once).\n\n- 94c82211 PERF (big): lightloop.js patches THREE.ShaderChunk.lights_fragment_begin at startup\n  (main.js calls cullPointLights() right after the imports) so a point light with\n  directLight.visible == false skips RE_Direct and its shadow lookup. Same picture; GPU frame\n  ~40-45 ms -> ~15-20 ms on the test machine. NOTE for three.js upgrades: it looks for\n  'getPointLightInfo( pointLight, geometryPosition, directLight );' and the next RE_Direct call;\n  does nothing if absent.\n\nMeasured: the meadow grass costs ~5.8-9.5 ms on this headless GPU at high quality looking across\nthe meadow (0.5 ms looking at the sky), and it scales with pixels (fragment-bound: shading the\nvisible blades with all the scene's lights). Drawing the tufts near-to-far made no measurable\ndifference (reverted). If frame time matters, the levers are the patch radius (quality.blades)\nor a cheaper lighting model for the blades.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"4fdb1492-f8b8-40a1-9a09-9682bfef3b26","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","root":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","branch":"hedgerow-grass","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":3,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"47ad52bf-d436-4572-912a-f84602d4848e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
