{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"d23553a2ceb0791fa9ed7db89cd7c442f7f2d51e0f0f35f5f6d58eaf74275846","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BxYmTHqebN1CBnySDos8nr","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/js/lights.js fun/hedgerow/js/main.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: a second shadow-casting lamp on high quality\n\nOn high quality the two strongest lamps or fires near the camera both\ncast shadows (the second at least 4 m from the first), so a soldier\nbetween two street lamps throws two shadows and a lamp's light no\nlonger leaks through the wall or sandbags beside the other. With the\nlight-loop culling in place it costs about 1-2.5 ms a frame on the\ntest GPU (it was 10-15 ms before). Medium and low are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && git merge-tree --write-tree hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null && echo \"merge with hedgerow-poc: clean\"","description":"Commit the second shadow light and check the merge"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
