{"parentUuid":"caf1b717-2b3e-4d67-b84e-7486d62762d8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgG7wq9468hiWR7TqhHXr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UNW4LSAF7HHjN7CNRdkRRy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='js/damage.js'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"   machine-gun fire stitched across plaster and stone. All of it is put down\n   at load from each building's own shape. A model's four sides are drawn\n   once, in software, into a grid of what is in front every 5 cm: how far\n   out, how squarely it faces that way, the colour of its texture there. A\n   mark goes only where the wall is open and flat across its whole size, so\n   never over a window, a beam, a drainpipe, a corner or the ivy, and a\n   plaster break only on plaster (light and plain). How many marks a wall\n   gets goes by how open the ground in front of it is and how near it is to\n   the lines the fighting follows. The marks are pinned decals in the bullet\n   holes' own meshes (atmosphere.js): no new draw calls, and the fighting\n   never wears them away. Seeded, so the village is the same every time. */\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"   machine-gun fire stitched across plaster and stone, now and then the\n   crater a cannon shell left. All of it is put down at load from each\n   building's own shape: a side of a model is drawn once (the first time a\n   wall needs it), in software, into a grid of what is in front every 5 cm:\n   how far out, how squarely it faces that way, the colour of its texture\n   there. A mark goes only where the wall is open and even across its whole\n   size, so never over a window, a shutter, a beam, a drainpipe, a corner or\n   the ivy, and a plaster break only on a house's plaster (light and plain).\n   How many marks a wall gets goes by how open the ground in front of it is\n   and how near that is to the lines the fighting follows. The marks are\n   pinned decals in the bullet holes' own meshes (atmosphere.js; the breaks\n   one more): the fighting never wears them away. Seeded, so the village is\n   the same every time. */\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='js/atmosphere.js'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"   a hole; mud thrown up in clods. Every kind is painted four ways (the\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"   a hole; mud thrown up in clods; and (only pinned, the walls' old damage,\n   damage.js) plaster broken off down to the stone or brick it was laid on.\n   Every kind is painted four ways (the\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nsed -n 160,176p js/atmosphere.js","description":"Update the module headers"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7831,"cache_read_input_tokens":417508,"output_tokens":1599,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":583},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7831,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1599,"cache_read_input_tokens":417508,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7831,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7831},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01UNW4LSAF7HHjN7CNRdkRRy":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='js/damage.js'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"   machine-gun fire stitched across plaster and stone. All of it is put down\n   at load from each building's own shape. A model's four sides are drawn\n   once, in software, into a grid of what is in front every 5 cm: how far\n   out, how squarely it faces that way, the colour of its texture there. A\n   mark goes only where the wall is open and flat across its whole size, so\n   never over a window, a beam, a drainpipe, a corner or the ivy, and a\n   plaster break only on plaster (light and plain). How many marks a wall\n   gets goes by how open the ground in front of it is and how near it is to\n   the lines the fighting follows. The marks are pinned decals in the bullet\n   holes' own meshes (atmosphere.js): no new draw calls, and the fighting\n   never wears them away. Seeded, so the village is the same every time. */\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"   machine-gun fire stitched across plaster and stone, now and then the\n   crater a cannon shell left. All of it is put down at load from each\n   building's own shape: a side of a model is drawn once (the first time a\n   wall needs it), in software, into a grid of what is in front every 5 cm:\n   how far out, how squarely it faces that way, the colour of its texture\n   there. A mark goes only where the wall is open and even across its whole\n   size, so never over a window, a shutter, a beam, a drainpipe, a corner or\n   the ivy, and a plaster break only on a house's plaster (light and plain).\n   How many marks a wall gets goes by how open the ground in front of it is\n   and how near that is to the lines the fighting follows. The marks are\n   pinned decals in the bullet holes' own meshes (atmosphere.js; the breaks\n   one more): the fighting never wears them away. Seeded, so the village is\n   the same every time. */\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='js/atmosphere.js'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"   a hole; mud thrown up in clods. Every kind is painted four ways (the\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"   a hole; mud thrown up in clods; and (only pinned, the walls' old damage,\n   damage.js) plaster broken off down to the stone or brick it was laid on.\n   Every kind is painted four ways (the\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nsed -n 160,176p js/atmosphere.js","description":"Update the module headers"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"140be1ea-50f7-424e-8565-2a0aee8877cc","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgG7wpcJoDmb5g4ifoXNL","requestRef":"776a39d3-685f-47e7-85ce-66f94b29032b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0f833422-8b39-4bfa-946e-11e134aa0835","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:50:06.491Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"0f833422-8b39-4bfa-946e-11e134aa0835","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6d5c0a1d-fdd5-4db0-8cbd-a5c82a0adcb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UNW4LSAF7HHjN7CNRdkRRy","type":"tool_result","content":"/* ---------- decals ---------- */\n\n/* What a bullet leaves, by what it hit, and the scorch of a blast. Each is a\n   small lit quad with a relief of its own (a normal map, so a lamp, a fire, a\n   flare or the muzzle flash picks out a crater's rim): stone chipped away pale\n   round a black hole, cracked and powdered; wood splintered along its grain,\n   the fresh wood showing; paint dented and flaked off to the bare steel round\n   a hole; mud thrown up in clods; and (only pinned, the walls' old damage,\n   damage.js) plaster broken off down to the stone or brick it was laid on.\n   Every kind is painted four ways (the\n   quarters of its textures), and each decal takes one at random, turned at\n   random. A bullet stops at a collider, a flat box, and a wall's stones bulge a\n   few centimetres out of it: so each decal is drawn pulled towards the eye\n   along its own sight line (it stays where it is on the screen) by PULL, which\n   brings it out over the stones instead of into them. */\n\nconst PULL = 0.06;","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2029685a-8358-4ffb-bb36-e941bd6e69c4","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:50:07.295Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"/* ---------- decals ---------- */\n\n/* What a bullet leaves, by what it hit, and the scorch of a blast. Each is a\n   small lit quad with a relief of its own (a normal map, so a lamp, a fire, a\n   flare or the muzzle flash picks out a crater's rim): stone chipped away pale\n   round a black hole, cracked and powdered; wood splintered along its grain,\n   the fresh wood showing; paint dented and flaked off to the bare steel round\n   a hole; mud thrown up in clods; and (only pinned, the walls' old damage,\n   damage.js) plaster broken off down to the stone or brick it was laid on.\n   Every kind is painted four ways (the\n   quarters of its textures), and each decal takes one at random, turned at\n   random. A bullet stops at a collider, a flat box, and a wall's stones bulge a\n   few centimetres out of it: so each decal is drawn pulled towards the eye\n   along its own sight line (it stays where it is on the screen) by PULL, which\n   brings it out over the stones instead of into them. */\n\nconst PULL = 0.06;","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"140be1ea-50f7-424e-8565-2a0aee8877cc","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"REDACTED","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":null,"remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}]},"error":"not_a_repo"},"live_cwd":"REDACTED","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0f833422-8b39-4bfa-946e-11e134aa0835","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
