{"parentUuid":"1085aa19-2515-4ad2-8c9a-b0e1e84d1453","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6d5c0a1d-fdd5-4db0-8cbd-a5c82a0adcb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XAqhnvDFwtN2dU9KNLfdwA","type":"tool_result","content":"/* What a bullet leaves, by what it hit, and the scorch of a blast. Each is a\n   small lit quad with a relief of its own (a normal map, so a lamp, a fire, a\n   flare or the muzzle flash picks out a crater's rim): stone chipped away pale\n   round a black hole, cracked and powdered; wood splintered along its grain,\n   the fresh wood showing; paint dented and flaked off to the bare steel round\n   a hole; mud thrown up in clods; and (only pinned, the walls' old damage,\n   damage.js) plaster broken off down to the stone or brick it was laid on.\n   Every kind is painted four ways (the quarters of its textures), and each\n   decal takes one at random, turned at random. A bullet stops at a collider,\n   a flat box, and a wall's stones bulge a\n   few centimetres out of it: so each decal is drawn pulled towards the eye\n   along its own sight line (it stays where it is on the screen) by PULL, which\n   brings it out over the stones instead of into them. */\n\nconst PULL = 0.06;\n52:halos in the wet air, low mist, bullet holes that catch the light — stone\n54:the bare steel — mud kicked up and the scorch of blasts, a low\n262:    (halos, mist, and decals: four painted variants of each kind with their","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"689d649b-10e1-4fd3-8f53-704e6e07b287","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:50:14.313Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"/* What a bullet leaves, by what it hit, and the scorch of a blast. Each is a\n   small lit quad with a relief of its own (a normal map, so a lamp, a fire, a\n   flare or the muzzle flash picks out a crater's rim): stone chipped away pale\n   round a black hole, cracked and powdered; wood splintered along its grain,\n   the fresh wood showing; paint dented and flaked off to the bare steel round\n   a hole; mud thrown up in clods; and (only pinned, the walls' old damage,\n   damage.js) plaster broken off down to the stone or brick it was laid on.\n   Every kind is painted four ways (the quarters of its textures), and each\n   decal takes one at random, turned at random. A bullet stops at a collider,\n   a flat box, and a wall's stones bulge a\n   few centimetres out of it: so each decal is drawn pulled towards the eye\n   along its own sight line (it stays where it is on the screen) by PULL, which\n   brings it out over the stones instead of into them. */\n\nconst PULL = 0.06;\n52:halos in the wet air, low mist, bullet holes that catch the light — stone\n54:the bare steel — mud kicked up and the scorch of blasts, a low\n262:    (halos, mist, and decals: four painted variants of each kind with their","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/js/atmosphere.js","hunks":[{"oldStart":166,"oldLines":9,"newStart":166,"newLines":9,"lines":["    the fresh wood showing; paint dented and flaked off to the bare steel round","    a hole; mud thrown up in clods; and (only pinned, the walls' old damage,","    damage.js) plaster broken off down to the stone or brick it was laid on.","-   Every kind is painted four ways (the","-   quarters of its textures), and each decal takes one at random, turned at","-   random. A bullet stops at a collider, a flat box, and a wall's stones bulge a","+   Every kind is painted four ways (the quarters of its textures), and each","+   decal takes one at random, turned at random. A bullet stops at a collider,","+   a flat box, and a wall's stones bulge a","    few centimetres out of it: so each decal is drawn pulled towards the eye","    along its own sight line (it stays where it is on the screen) by PULL, which","    brings it out over the stones instead of into them. */"]}]}],"moreFiles"