{"parentUuid":"49a2929c-a404-4a3e-ba94-8a31ac473437","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6d5c0a1d-fdd5-4db0-8cbd-a5c82a0adcb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TwUR4doT17htZYLiQ9rJJh","type":"tool_result","content":"them in stretches, rainwater standing in the shell craters — rain in fine\nstreaks, falling in sheets far down the street, sweeping across in gusts,\ndripping and pouring in broken strings off the eaves, lit by lamps, fires\nand flares,\nhalos in the wet air, low mist, bullet holes that catch the light — stone\nchipped pale round a black hole, wood splintered, paint flaked off a dent to\nthe bare steel — mud kicked up and the scorch of blasts, a low\ncloud deck rolling overhead, its bellies lit orange from below over the\nburning farms, whose smoke climbs into it in leaning columns, and caught by\nthe flashes of a distant barrage, searchlights sweeping\nthe cloud over the front and flak tracer going up into it, and every half minute\nor so an illumination flare going up over the front and sinking under its\nparachute, lighting the cloud, glittering on the wet cobbles and laying long\n    blast's fireball: a billboard whose shader swells a ball of turbulent\n    flame in a tenth of a second, yellow at its heart and orange in its\n    folds, cooling from the outside in to a dull red glow inside a ball of\n    smoke that rolls up and thins into the blast's dust), `atmosphere.js`\n    (halos, mist, and decals: four painted variants of each kind with their\n    own relief, drawn pulled a few centimetres towards the eye along their\n    sight line so a wall's stones do not swallow them), `casings.js` (the\n    brass thrown out of the gun — the Garand's long bottlenecked case, the\n    Thompson's short one — tumbling past in the muzzle flash, bouncing and\n    lying where it falls; the last 64 of each stay), `chunks.js` (what a\n    blast throws up: clods of mud and turf, or stones off the cobbles, as\n    solid lumps that tumble, knock off walls, bounce and lie where they\n    fall),\n    `audio.js` (procedural, nothing downloaded; foley: steps by what is\n    underfoot — hobnails on stone, sucking mud, swishing grass, crackling","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"64f28b92-d05a-4e22-b4e2-bc8d0c8afbe8","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:50:19.865Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"them in stretches, rainwater standing in the shell craters — rain in fine\nstreaks, falling in sheets far down the street, sweeping across in gusts,\ndripping and pouring in broken strings off the eaves, lit by lamps, fires\nand flares,\nhalos in the wet air, low mist, bullet holes that catch the light — stone\nchipped pale round a black hole, wood splintered, paint flaked off a dent to\nthe bare steel — mud kicked up and the scorch of blasts, a low\ncloud deck rolling overhead, its bellies lit orange from below over the\nburning farms, whose smoke climbs into it in leaning columns, and caught by\nthe flashes of a distant barrage, searchlights sweeping\nthe cloud over the front and flak tracer going up into it, and every half minute\nor so an illumination flare going up over the front and sinking under its\nparachute, lighting the cloud, glittering on the wet cobbles and laying long\n    blast's fireball: a billboard whose shader swells a ball of turbulent\n    flame in a tenth of a second, yellow at its heart and orange in its\n    folds, cooling from the outside in to a dull red glow inside a ball of\n    smoke that rolls up and thins into the blast's dust), `atmosphere.js`\n    (halos, mist, and decals: four painted variants of each kind with their\n    own relief, drawn pulled a few centimetres towards the eye along their\n    sight line so a wall's stones do not swallow them), `casings.js` (the\n    brass thrown out of the gun — the Garand's long bottlenecked case, the\n    Thompson's short one — tumbling past in the muzzle flash, bouncing and\n    lying where it falls; the last 64 of each stay), `chunks.js` (what a\n    blast throws up: clods of mud and turf, or stones off the cobbles, as\n    solid lumps that tumble, knock off walls, bounce and lie where they\n    fall),\n    `audio.js` (procedural, nothing downloaded; foley: steps by what is\n    underfoot — hobnails on stone, sucking mud, swishing grass, crackling","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/js/atmosphere.js","hunks":[{"oldStart":168,"oldLines":10,"newStart":168,"newLines":10,"lines":["    damage.js) plaster broken off down to the stone or brick it was laid on.","    Every kind is painted four ways (the quarters of its textures), and each","    decal takes one at random, turned at random. A bullet stops at a collider,","-   a flat box, and a wall's stones bulge a","-   few centimetres out of it: so each decal is drawn pulled towards the eye","-   along its own sight line (it stays where it is on the screen) by PULL, which","-   brings it out over the stones instead of into them. */","+   a flat box, and a wall's stones bulge a few centimetres out of it: so each","+   decal is drawn pulled towards the eye along its own sight line (it stays","+   where it is on the screen) by PULL, which brings it out over the stones","+   instead of into them. */"," "," const PULL = 0.06;"," const FLAT = 160; // a relief's surface, on its height canvas (lower is sunk in)"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/js/atmosphere.js"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"eab3766f-57a8-46bc-aebc-3a92ce4149f5","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","root":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","branch":"hedgerow-grass","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"un