{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","id":"7584a708-7861-4139-b8fa-f74392a2b93e","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:52:12.979Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"aca1d33e67df77c08846866245a8b157faabfdb8617ed3a1eb9cac3e5556c296","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"max"}},"base":"f5d96a9a-c849-4bd9-9adf-c0e950b79b4f","keep":437,"tail":["f209da63c444d5d7833ecf43b7e4f2ba2652e8e961fdf941e749a71643d4099f","3c16f7a98c09c67ef611b901d55ea458545a4cdbf1bb649129c3e55a5e735218","d59c67b2a4dffc98304ed16981225a89f9f1fc22ddf1f5bfb5e57f669f0d0973"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",439,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"a15ac53dcff794af1a8b4f75364446d98e99bfc76f707acbe110b52450f7193f"}
{"parentUuid":"a331b026-b398-4061-8641-4eed31229cd2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgG88DFNBJvLT3rBkAkEM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This round added three commits to `hedgerow-grass`, none pushed: 94c82211, 8dcfc434 and 6bbd4fff. Node checks pass, shaders compile on low, medium and high, and the merge with `hedgerow-poc` is still clean.\n\n- **94c82211 – lights only where they reach** (`lightloop.js`): three.js was shading all nine point lights on every pixel, even where a light's range had cut it to nothing. Skipping those pixels gives the same picture with frames about 2.5× faster on the test GPU (street 43 → 17–21 ms).\n- **8dcfc434 – a second shadow-casting lamp, high quality only**: the two strongest lamps or fires near you both cast shadows, so a lamp's light no longer leaks through the wall beside the other. I had dropped this earlier at +10–15 ms a frame; after the culling it costs about 1–2.5 ms.\n- **6bbd4fff – walls scarred by earlier fighting** (new `damage.js`): the village walls were spotless. At load, walls facing open ground near the street, lane and track now get:\n  - plaster blown off down to rubble stone or brick;\n  - cannon-shell craters;\n  - machine-gun bursts.\n  \n  Each building's sides are drawn in software into a 5 cm grid, so marks only land on open, even wall, never across a window, shutter or corner. They are pinned decals that gameplay hits never overwrite. That comes to about 30 breaks and 200 holes, adding roughly 190 ms to loading, with GPU cost within measurement noise.\n\nThings to know:\n- The house fronts are mostly windows and open shutters, so most plaster breaks land on the gable ends; the fronts mainly get bullet holes.\n- Breaks show clearly up close and at about 13 m, but they're easy to miss from the middle of the street. More density or larger breaks are an option if you want the damage more obvious.\n\nThe headless browser and preview server are stopped, no browser tabs are open, and my `launch.json` entry is removed. Notes are in the shared notes file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":517,"cache_read_input_tokens":438613,"output_tokens":689,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":517,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":689,"cache_read_input_tokens":438613,"cache_creation_input_tokens":517,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":517},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"3d550230-642a-41d3-82eb-4477cdd46296","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgG88CjcBK6bxkKadHuBS","requestRef":"7584a708-7861-4139-b8fa-f74392a2b93e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"fd521167-e8ad-4fbb-bad5-aafe69e03f43","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:52:20.200Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
